<mxCell id="s48" value="48. Push FCM/APNS&#10;New email from sender" style="html=1;verticalAlign=bottom;endArrow=block;strokeWidth=2;strokeColor=#ef6c00;fontSize=10" edge="1" parent="1" source="notifLine" target="userLine"><mxGeometry width="80" relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

<mxCell id="interview" value="INTERVIEW KEY QUESTIONS: Q1: Why INSERT outbox BEFORE Kafka publish? A1: Atomic transaction guarantees email survives crash. If Kafka succeeds but server dies before DB commit → email lost. Outbox pattern: INSERT outbox + Kafka publish in SAME transaction → both succeed or both rollback. Email durable in DB, retry from outbox on restart. Q2: How determine SLA priority HIGH vs NORMAL vs LOW? A2: Same domain gmail→gmail OR recipient in contacts OR VIP sender → HIGH priority Kafka topic email.smtp.high, 50 workers target &lt;1min. External first-time OR no urgent keywords → NORMAL topic, 100 workers 5min. Bulk 100+ recipients OR List-Unsubscribe header → LOW topic, 20 workers 30min rate limited. Q3: SPF/DKIM/DMARC authentication flow? A3: SPF: receiver queries DNS dig TXT gmail.com → v=spf1 ip4:74.125... → checks sender IP in range → PASS or FAIL. DKIM: email has DKIM-Signature header with signature → receiver fetches public key dig TXT default._domainkey.gmail.com → verifies signature matches content → PASS prevents tampering. DMARC: dig TXT _dmarc.gmail.com → p=reject policy → checks SPF or DKIM alignment with From domain → if both FAIL → 550 reject, if p=quarantine → spam folder. All three block spoofing. Q4: Retry strategy on SMTP failure? A4: Exponential backoff: 1min → 5min → 15min → max 10 attempts over 24hr. Temporary failures 4xx codes (421 Service unavailable, 450 Mailbox busy) → retry. Permanent failures 5xx codes (550 User not found, 552 Mailbox full) → stop retry, send bounce notification to sender, mark status=FAILED. DLQ after 10 attempts for manual investigation. Idempotency: receiver deduplicates by Message-ID header prevents duplicate delivery. Q5: Why S3 for attachments not DB? A5: 25MB attachment × 1B emails = 25 petabytes in PostgreSQL = disaster. DB buffer pool contamination (attachment bytes evict hot index pages). Backup disaster (restore weeks). S3 solution: upload to S3, store only URL in DB. 11 nines durability, lifecycle Glacier after 1yr saves 90% cost, presigned URLs direct upload/download bypass server." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e3f2fd;strokeColor=#1976d2;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=10" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="60" y="1760" width="2480" height="20" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

</root></mxGraphModel></diagram></mxfile>
